With Red Hat 9 being released to the open source community as the Fedora
project, will SELinux development continue with the Fedora core only, will
SELinux development continue with Red Hat Enterprise Linux only, or will
SELinux development continue with both?.  It seems that SELinux changes are
being upstreamed to rawhide for release with the 2.6 kernel.  Will this
kernel, along with upstreamed changes to glibc, be included in Fedora's
release later this year as well as the next release of RH Enterprise?  With
Fedora being an open source community supported project, will this introduce
security risks of backdoors being introduced into the core?

